<%# How a secret's steps are written (Clue), for the GM's and the setting's forms. %>
One per line, vaguest first, the first a question. A clue someone tells says who after <code>|</code>, so clues can disagree.
Each clue the party finds gives them the next, wherever they found it: an uncover, the place, the person, or the GM; after the last, the secret itself.
Story rows can ask how far the party has got by its key: <code>goblin_silver >= 1</code>, <code>!goblin_silver_known</code>.
